        "title": "fix(providers): publish Meta under canonical package name",
        "body": "Related: #102873\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where the newly merged Meta provider used the internal `meta-model-api` name and could not be published through the official npm or ClawHub release paths.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nRenames the unshipped provider surface to `meta`, publishes it as `@openclaw/meta-provider`, and adds the package, catalog, documentation, label, shrinkwrap, and release metadata required by both registries. The provider remains bundled in OpenClaw.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can select models as `meta/muse-spark-1.1`, configure Meta with `--meta-api-key`, and install the standalone provider from npm or ClawHub when needed.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Testbox `tbx_01kx40dk128p77xzyj7sc3ewk7`: 162 focused assertions passed across the provider, official catalog, npm release, ClawHub release, and live-shard routing.\n- Testbox `tbx_01kx41enjnj1txqm7c9y7wr0kd`: rebuilt the package runtime and produced a clean 12-file `@openclaw/meta-provider@2026.6.11` npm tarball preview.\n- `plugin-npm-release-check`: selected `@openclaw/meta-provider@2026.6.11`.\n- `plugin-clawhub-release-check`: selected `@openclaw/meta-provider@2026.6.11`.\n- npm shrinkwrap, plugin inventory, docs map, and `git diff --check` are clean.\n- Fresh Codex autoreview reported no accepted or actionable findings.\n",
